      "id": "sequential-calls",
      "text": "Start with two distinct zero-value Once instances. Call Do on the first with a callback that returns normally, then call Do on it again with a different callback. The first callback runs once and the second is skipped. Calling Do on the other instance with the second callback runs it there. If the first callback records an initialization error and returns normally, the same instance still skips subsequent callbacks. The contract requires a fresh instance and prohibits copying a Once after first use.",
